WEBVTT

00:00:08,820 --> 00:00:18,020
I have a very old computer for my rife. I think it's a Windows 7 that I got from you about 15

00:00:18,020 --> 00:00:23,380
years ago and I started with you. Should I replace it? It seems to be working just fine.

00:00:25,300 --> 00:00:33,780
No, you shouldn't replace it. Quite honestly, some of those old computers back 15 years ago

00:00:34,420 --> 00:00:44,740
were better quality than the ones you could purchase today. I have a number of people that started

00:00:44,740 --> 00:00:52,100
with me 15, 20 years ago that are still using the Windows 7 computer that came with their rife,

00:00:52,100 --> 00:01:01,380
and it still works, which is a testimony for a little laptop. So don't you don't need to replace it,

00:01:01,380 --> 00:01:10,260
don't just keep going with it. There's no reason to replace it. I think every single person

00:01:10,980 --> 00:01:18,580
I've updated their program to be a true rife now. I've updated their program to be version 6 or

00:01:18,580 --> 00:01:25,380
version 6.4, which is you don't need anything beyond that. Still have some people that are still

00:01:25,380 --> 00:01:30,100
not in version 5.5, but it's working just fine and it's working with their program to

00:01:30,100 --> 00:01:34,980
find that they've been in remission for 15 years, so I don't think we need to change anything.

